      "DISAMBIGUATION NOTE (research 2026-07-03): this Ann Austin (b. 3 Apr 1703 Evesham, Burlington Co., NJ; m. Josiah Albertson 1727; d. 1767 Gloucester, NJ) is a distinct person from the well-known Quaker missionary Ann Austin who, with Mary Fisher, was the first Quaker imprisoned in Boston in 1656 — that Ann Austin was already \"stricken in years\" with five children by 1656, decades before this Ann Austin was born. Flagged only to prevent future confusion given the shared name and Quaker affiliation; not a correction to this record's own data."
